{
  "_comment": [
    "Cross-language golden vectors for the traffic wire format. Read by both",
    "libs/traffic/traffic_tests/traffic_info_test.cpp (UNIT_TEST(TrafficInfo_GoldenVectors))",
    "and tools/traffic_server/test/wire.test.ts, so the C++ client and the TypeScript server",
    "cannot drift apart.",
    "",
    "keysHex is the complete .traffic.keys body (uncompressed).",
    "valuesPlainHex is the values payload BEFORE zlib deflation -- zlib output is",
    "implementation-defined and must not be goldened.",
    "",
    "The 'mixed' case is taken from UNIT_TEST(TrafficInfo_Serialization) and covers one-way and",
    "two-way features, a multi-segment feature, and fid = 2^32-1."
  ],
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "mixed",
      "features": [
        { "fid": 0, "numSegs": 1, "oneWay": true },
        { "fid": 1, "numSegs": 1, "oneWay": false },
        { "fid": 5, "numSegs": 2, "oneWay": false },
        { "fid": 4294967295, "numSegs": 1, "oneWay": true }
      ],
      "keys": [
        [0, 0, 0],
        [1, 0, 0],
        [1, 0, 1],
        [5, 0, 0],
        [5, 0, 1],
        [5, 1, 0],
        [5, 1, 1],
        [4294967295, 0, 0]
      ],
      "values": ["G0", "G1", "G3", "G2", "G2", "G2", "G5", "TempBlock"],
      "keysHex": "0004c500000000f7ffffff9295",
      "valuesPlainHex": "0008c824d5"
    },
    {
      "name": "empty",
      "features": [],
      "keys": [],
      "values": [],
